# The lead's records are append-only logs that two Macs' leads both add to. git's built-in union driver keeps both
# sides' lines where they overlap, so a merge of main between them never stops on a conflict (2026-10-31, 2026-11-02).
docs/lead/progress.md merge=union
docs/lead/decisions.md merge=union
# Workers that edit a file shared with main each add a row at the end of the v2 port map's Non-seam edits table; two
# such branches conflicted there alone, and each then needed a new commit, audit and approval (three times on
# 2026-11-19). The union driver keeps both rows. It keeps both versions of a row two branches edit differently too:
# PortMapLintTests finds those (two rows with one name), a row left outside its table and a short row.
docs/process/v2-port-map.md merge=union
